{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/recipes.md .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/acceptance.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/recipes.md .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/acceptance.md'","aggregated_output":"# Atomic recipes\n\n`taskspec recipe list` discovers pinned strategies. `recipe show <strategy>` emits\na resolved example; `recipe validate <file> --budget <n>` validates a resolved\nrecipe. TaskPlan units accept either a strategy name or a resolved recipe mapping.\nNative authored decomposition recipes accept strategy names.\n\nBind acceptance checks to the source requirements and recorded decisions. If a\nlimit, threshold, or edge-case behavior is unspecified, label a proposed choice\nand keep it open for review; do not encode it as an already agreed requirement.\n\nDuring authoring, choose scratch paths before running eval-discrimination checks.\nIf the harness confines file tools to the workspace, create a unique scratch\nsubdirectory under the initiative's planning workspace and remove only the scratch\nfiles created by that check. A system temporary directory is not automatically\nwithin the permitted write surface. Once execution is sealed, scratch writes must\nalso fit the signed task scope. A denied write stops the session; this guidance\nnever authorizes moving that denied action to another path.\n\nFor a directly authored TaskPlan with multiline shell evals, use a JSON manifest\nand encode each command as a JSON string with `\\n` escapes. The portable YAML\nmanifest reader supports a restricted subset and does not accept `|` or `>` block\nscalars. Multiline commands remain supported through JSON; direct atomic-task\nauthoring also remains available.\n\nStrategies are direct, plan-execute-verify, diagnose-repair-verify, test-first, and\nresearch-synthesize-verify. Their guidance resolves into the Validation Card's\nagent contract before HMAC authorization. Changing installed strategy instructions\ncannot alter a sealed task. Use relevant context, examples when needed, tool\nfeedback, explicit deliverables, and concise self-checks; do not request private\nreasoning transcripts.\n\nEach recipe stays within one outcome, scope, authority, and timeout. Internal\nsteps are sequential. Independent ownership or acceptance requires another leaf.\nNew recipes default to three executor-plus-evaluation rounds and stop after two\nidentical failing-eval/write-digest observations, capped by the signed budget.\nTimeout and consumed rounds persist across replacement attempts of the same\nrevision. Cancellation, stale authorization, scope escape, and unavailable required\nenforcement stop work. Optional usage metrics remain null when unavailable.\n# First accepted task and evidence\n\nFor one small understood change, author `TaskPlan/v1`, preview it with\n`taskspec plan --manifest <file>`, and materialize with `taskspec batch --plan <file>`.\nInspect `taskspec validate <spec>`, `taskspec dod <spec>`, and every eval. An eval\nmust discriminate a real result from a stub; metadata compliance is not behavioral proof.\n\nRecord human authorization with `taskspec gate --stamp <spec> --stamp-by <identity>`.\nFor ordinary tasks, create an attempt handoff using\n`taskspec handoff <spec> --backend <backend> --out <path>`, execute within it, and\nuse canonical `taskspec accept --handoff <path> --stamp <spec>` with the required\nreceipts and supervisor decision. For managed recipes use the Mesh route in the\nexecution guide. Failed evals, stale revisions, and missing required attestations\ncannot establish acceptance. Never edit sealed evals to make work pass.\n\n`taskspec status --initiative <id>` reconstructs acceptance from canonical records,\nseparately from lifecycle status. `graph --initiative <id> --view capabilities`\nshows explicit integration proof gaps. Passing child tasks does not prove a capability,\na successful pipeline does not establish service health, and acceptance does not\nauthorize production release.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md; git status --short; rg --files -g \"!node_modules\" -g \"!.git\" -g \"!.agents\" -g \"!.codex\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md; git status --short; rg --files -g \"!node_modules\" -g \"!.git\" -g \"!.agents\" -g \"!.codex\"'","aggregated_output":"# Chat qualification fixture\n\nUse the installed task-spec skill at .agents/skills/task-spec/SKILL.md.\nThe version-matched TaskSpec CLI is `bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-649884a-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\"`.\nThis is a fresh conversation: derive current state from artifacts.\nFollow the user request within this repository. Do not spawn agents, commit, publish, or change the installed engine.\n# Rate-limiting steel thread (test evidence fixture)\n\nSynthetic evidence source for `rate-limiting-recipe.yaml`. It exists so the\nproving fixture has a real local file to hash, and so source verification,\ndigest mismatch, and tamper rejection can be exercised without depending on\na large binary document.\n\n## Steel thread order\n\n1. A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n2. Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n3. Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n4. The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope.\n- Production storage and deployment infrastructure are not selected here.\n\nThis file is fixture input. It is not documentation of shipped behavior.\nCLAUDE.md\nAGENTS.md\ntests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-649884a-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\" agent-context'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-649884a-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\" agent-context'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"contract\": \"TaskSpecAgentContext/v1\",\n  \"engine_version\": \"3.10.0\",\n  \"format_version\": 4,\n  \"default_format_version\": 3,\n  \"supported_format_versions\": [\n    1,\n    2,\n    3,\n    4\n  ],\n  \"binary\": \"taskspec\",\n  \"global_options\": {\n    \"--json\": \"wrap command stdout/stderr and exit status in one JSON envelope\",\n    \"--dry-run\": \"prevent supported mutations and report intended action\",\n    \"NO_COLOR\": \"disable ANSI color when present\",\n    \"TASKSPEC_COLOR\": \"0 disables and 1 forces ANSI color\"\n  },\n  \"exit_codes\": {\n    \"0\": \"success\",\n    \"1\": \"validation, gate, eval, or acceptance failure\",\n    \"2\": \"usage error\",\n    \"3\": \"unsupported runtime requirement\"\n  },\n  \"commands\": {\n    \"init\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"INIT=OK\",\n        \"INIT=DRY_RUN\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec init [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\"\n    },\n    \"setup\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"SETUP=READY\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec setup | taskspec setup signing [--force] | taskspec setup decompose\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"setup signing\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec setup signing\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\"\n    },\n    \"demo\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DEMO=READY\",\n        \"DEMO=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"DEMO=BLOCKED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec demo\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\"\n    },\n    \"example\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec example task-plan --out <file> [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\"\n    },\n    \"new\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec new [--format 3|4] [--status ready|blocked] [--queue] <slug> <XS|S|M|L|XL|XXL> [agent] [source-note]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--format\",\n        \"--queue\",\n        \"--status\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\"\n    },\n    \"plan\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TASK_PLAN=OK\",\n        \"TASK_PLAN=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec plan --manifest <TaskPlan.yaml>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--manifest\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"batch\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TASK_BATCH=OK\",\n        \"TASK_BATCH=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"TASK_BATCH=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec batch --plan <TaskPlan.yaml> | taskspec batch --intent-file <file> --effort <size>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--effort\",\n        \"--intent-file\",\n        \"--plan\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\"\n    },\n    \"migrate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec migrate <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\"\n    },\n    \"validate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec validate [--no-state] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--no-state\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\"\n    },\n    \"dod\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DOD=COMPLETE\",\n        \"DOD=GAPS\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec dod <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"gate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TIER=1\",\n        \"TIER=2\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec gate [--stamp] [--require-tier1] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--require-tier\",\n        \"--stamp\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\"\n    },\n    \"handoff\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"HANDOFF=WRITTEN\",\n        \"HANDOFF=INVALID\",\n        \"HANDOFF=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec handoff <task-spec> --backend <token> [--out <file>] [--attempt-id <uuid>]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--attempt-id\",\n        \"--backend\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\"\n    },\n    \"run\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec run [--ci] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--ci\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\"\n    },\n    \"accept\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"ACCEPTED=1\",\n        \"ACCEPTED=0\",\n        \"ACCEPTANCE_FAILURE=<code>\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec accept [--stamp] [--handoff <file>] [receipt flags] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--handoff\",\n        \"--stamp\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\"\n    },\n    \"author-doctor\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"AUTHOR_DOCTOR=READY\",\n        \"AUTHOR_DOCTOR=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec author-doctor <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"holdout\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"HOLDOUT=SEALED\",\n        \"HOLDOUT=VERIFIED\",\n        \"HOLDOUT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec holdout seal|verify|run ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"receipt\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"RECEIPT=WRITTEN\",\n        \"RECEIPT=SIGNED\",\n        \"RECEIPT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec receipt validate|sign|engine|environment|evaluation|graded|human ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"eval-audit\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EVAL_AUDIT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec eval-audit <task-spec> --baseline <git-ref> [--mutations <matrix>] [--repeat N]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--baseline\",\n        \"--mutations\",\n        \"--repeat\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\"\n    },\n    \"identity\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"IDENTITY=READY\",\n        \"IDENTITY=SIGNED\",\n        \"IDENTITY=VERIFIED\",\n        \"IDENTITY=REVOKED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec identity init|sign|verify|revoke ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"ENGINE_MATRIX=VALID\",\n        \"ENGINE_MATRIX=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec evidence validate|plan|run <EngineMatrix.json> ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\"\n    },\n    \"bridge\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"BRIDGE=VALID\",\n        \"BRIDGE=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec bridge export|validate ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"dsse\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DSSE=EXPORTED\",\n        \"DSSE=VERIFIED\",\n        \"DSSE=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec dsse export|verify ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"mcp\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"read-only stdio server\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mcp\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"read-only stdio server\"\n    },\n    \"mesh\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"MESH_WATCH_READY\",\n        \"MESH_SUPERVISED_ACCEPTED\",\n        \"MESH_FINISHED\",\n        \"TASKMESH_ERROR=<code>\",\n        \"TASKMESH_DRY_RUN\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh <init|doctor|serve|frontier|run|status|watch|explain|cancel|resume|accept|finish|adapters|setup|mcp> ... | taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> [--execute]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--execute\",\n        \"--initiative\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\"\n    },\n    \"ready\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec ready [--all] [filters]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--all\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"graph\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"GRAPH=<digest>\",\n        \"GRAPH=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec graph [--task <id>] [--check] [--mermaid] [--json] | taskspec graph --initiative <id> --view tasks|capabilities\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--check\",\n        \"--initiative\",\n        \"--json\",\n        \"--mermaid\",\n        \"--task\",\n        \"--view\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"NEXT=<command>\",\n        \"STATUS=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec status <task-id-or-path> [--json] | taskspec status --initiative <id>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--initiative\",\n        \"--json\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\"\n    },\n    \"lint\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec lint\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"transition\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"changes lifecycle status and derived state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec transition <task-id> <ready|in-progress|blocked|done|parked> [reason]\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"changes lifecycle status and derived state\"\n    },\n    \"rebuild-state\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"rewrites deterministic tasks/_state.yaml\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec rebuild-state\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"rewrites deterministic tasks/_state.yaml\"\n    },\n    \"archive\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"moves root done/parked tasks under the task-state lock and refreshes derived state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec archive\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"moves root done/parked tasks under the task-state lock and refreshes derived state\"\n    },\n    \"backup\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes a timestamped backlog archive to the selected destination\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec backup [destination-directory]\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"writes a timestamped backlog archi