{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-649884a-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\" new --format 3 --status blocked policy-schema S any tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md'","aggregated_output":"Spec written: tasks/T-20260915-policy-schema.md\n  status: blocked  format: 3  outdir: tasks  task_spec_version: 3.10.0\n\nNext steps:\n\n  1. Fill in the {{TODO}} stubs:\n     - title\n     - touches_paths\n     - why / goal / context\n     - eval_1, eval_2, eval_3 (runnable bash — avoid the inverted-grep-c\n       footgun; use '! grep -q PATTERN file' instead of '$(grep -c X file\n       || echo 0); [ \"$count\" -eq 0 ]')\n     - anti-patterns + do-not-touch\n\n  2. VALIDATE (pre-gate structural linter — does NOT stamp signed_off):\n     taskspec validate tasks/T-20260915-policy-schema.md\n\nNext: taskspec gate --stamp tasks/T-20260915-policy-schema.md\n\n     The gate is THE only path to signed_off:true. Hand-stamping the\n     signed_off field is rejected by the structural sign-off envelope check.\n     See: docs/concepts/signed-off.md\n\n  3. DISPATCH (after the gate stamps signed_off:true):\n     See runbooks/dispatching-a-task-spec.md for the handoff protocol\n     per execution_backend (kimi, claude, codex, taskship, ...).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
